legalExplanation:
The **National Drug Law Enforcement Agency Act, section 41** gives authorised officers power, without warrant, to:
- enter and search any land, building or carrier they have reason to believe is connected with an offence under the Act;
- test and take samples of substances;
- arrest a person they have reason to believe committed an offence under the Act;
- seize any item or substance they have reason to believe was used in the commission of an offence.

**Section 41(2)** requires that **a written receipt of the Agency shall be given for any item, substance or thing seized** under the section.

Section 42 also allows the Agency, with the Attorney-General's written approval, to seek a freezing order over bank accounts linked to an arrested person where there is reason to believe the money came from drug trafficking.
